messages:
Maya: quick q — running into funky SSE behaviour in our node client when partial JSON objects arrive split across chunks. sometimes the auth refresh triggers a reconnect and we get half an object then a retry that resumes and app crashes with 'Unexpected end of JSON input'. anyone seen a pattern or recommended strategy for resuming without losing buffered partials?

Eli: yep. typical pattern is keep a rolling buffer and only JSON.parse complete objects. NDJSON framing helps — treat newline as delimiter. if events are framed like `data: {...}\n\n` you can split on double newline. otherwise use a streaming json parser (clarinet/oboe) for partial callbacks.

Maya: we are using plain text chunks, events aren't ndjson: server sends SSE with `data:` lines that can contain JSON that may be split mid-object. tried naive `buffer += chunk; const parts = buffer.split('\n\n')` but last part can be partial and we were discarding it incorrectly on reconnect.

Kai: don't drop the leftover on reconnect. persist buffer across reconnects until you either parse it or decide to discard on auth failure. also watch for multibyte utf8 split — use Buffer.concat and toString('utf8') carefully.

Jordan: small pseudo I used:

```
let buf = ''
stream.on('data', c => {
  buf += c.toString('utf8')
  let idx
  while ((idx = buf.indexOf('\n\n')) !== -1) {
    const frame = buf.slice(0, idx)
    buf = buf.slice(idx + 2)
    // extract data: lines
    const body = frame.split('\n').filter(l => l.startsWith('data:')).map(l => l.slice(5)).join('\n')
    try { const obj = JSON.parse(body); handle(obj) } catch (e) { console.warn('partial json, keep buffering') }
  }
})

// on reconnect, do NOT reset buf unless explicitly validated
```

Eli: also add a short timeout when waiting for completion (e.g., 30s) then surface error. and add an id field in events so on retry you can dedup/patch state rather than reapply.

Maya: thanks. one more: our auth refresh happens in the same process and we reconstruct the stream; during that gap some events are lost. any pattern to replay missing events? we have no ordered cursor.

Kai: if you can, include sequence numbers in the protocol. if not, best-effort is to backfill via REST for important ops. otherwise make your client idempotent so replay doesn't break things.

Maya: sending a tiny PR with the buffer-preserve change and a unit test for split multibyte boundary. ping @Eli @Jordan for review. also added a log flag `DEBUG_SSE` to show raw chunks.

Eli: will review shortly.

